{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"f0cd0785","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.005817,"end_time":"2026-10-19T17:22:22.888624+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T17:22:22.882807+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# House Price Prediction Using Machine Learning\n","\n","## Project Overview\n","\n","This project focuses on predicting residential house sale prices using machine learning regression techniques. It uses the **House Prices: Advanced Regression Techniques** dataset from Kaggle, which contains various features describing residential properties, including their size, quality, location-related characteristics, and construction details.\n","\n","The objective is to build and evaluate regression models that accurately predict house sale prices and compare their performance using cross-validation.\n","\n","The project explores data preprocessing, exploratory data analysis, target transformation, regression algorithms, and ensemble learning to develop a competitive predictive model.\n","\n","**Competition:** [House Prices: Advanced Regression Techniques](https://www.kaggle.com/competitions/house-prices-advanced-regression-techniques)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b83f1dd1","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.005187,"end_time":"2026-10-19T17:22:22.898708+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T17:22:22.893521+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Problem Statement\n","\n","The goal is to predict the final sale price of residential properties based on their observable characteristics.\n","\n","This is a **supervised regression problem** because the training dataset contains labeled examples with `SalePrice` as the target variable.\n","\n","The main objectives are:\n","\n","- Understand the relationship between property features and sale prices.\n","- Identify and handle missing values.\n","- Explore numerical and categorical variables.\n","- Prepare the dataset for machine learning.\n","- Train and compare multiple regression models.\n","- Evaluate performance using five-fold cross-validation.\n","- Combine model predictions through ensemble learning.\n","- Generate predictions for the competition's test dataset."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"7037df8d","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.004615,"end_time":"2026-10-19T17:22:22.907974+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T17:22:22.903359+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 1. Import Libraries and Load Data\n","\n","The project uses Python and its data science ecosystem for data manipulation, visualization, preprocessing, and model development.\n","\n","The main libraries include:\n","\n","- **NumPy:** Numerical operations and mathematical transformations.\n","- **Pandas:** Data loading, cleaning, and manipulation.\n","- **Matplotlib and Seaborn:** Exploratory data visualization.\n","- **Scikit-learn:** Data preprocessing, regression models, pipelines, and cross-validation.\n","- **LightGBM:** Gradient boosting using decision trees.\n","\n","The competition provides separate training and test datasets. The training dataset contains the target variable `SalePrice`, while the test dataset is used to generate final predictions."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"ad68313a","metadata":{"_cell_guid":"b1076dfc-b9ad-4769-8c92-a6c4dae69d19","_uuid":"8f2839f25d086af736a60e9eeb907d3b93b6e0e5","execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-19T17:22:22.919235Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-19T17:22:22.91889Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-19T17:22:25.250063Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-19T17:22:25.249123Z"},"papermill":{"duration":2.339459,"end_time":"2026-10-19T17:22:25.252204+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-10-19T17:22:22.912745+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["/kaggle/input/competitions/house-prices-advanced-regression-techniques/sample_submission.csv\n","/kaggle/input/competitions/house-prices-a